{"content_hash": "5a3be72701c7f6a0", "version_id": 724, "article_id": 73, "level_code": "en_b2", "lang": "en", "level": 4, "level_label": "B2 中高级", "title": "Paddy Power owner Flutter cuts 1,400 jobs over betting tax", "title_zh": "博彩税上涨，Paddy Power母公司Flutter裁员1400人", "has_translation": true, "topic": "business", "source": "bbc_business", "source_url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cqzrdpkm3g84o?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1567471945851-460fd29a04a2?ixid=M3wxMDk3Mzk1fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8OHx8cGFkZHklMjBwb3dlciUyMGN1dHN8ZW58MHwwfHx8MTc5MjU0MDk0M3ww&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&w=1600&q=75&fm=jpg&fit=max", "provider": "unsplash", "credit": "Photo by DANSHEN SOMINTAC on Unsplash", "author": "DANSHEN SOMINTAC", "credit_url": "https://unsplash.com/@danshen?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "source": "Unsplash", "source_url": "https://unsplash.com/photos/person-walking-on-corn-field-ncQT35ckj6o?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "fallback": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(133, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(171, 46%, 48%)", "label": "BUSINESS", "seed": "b1b57f6a7576"}}, "published_date": "2026-10-21", "word_count": 244, "reading_minutes": 1.2, "lead": "Flutter, the company behind Paddy Power, Sky Bet and Betfair, is cutting up to 1,400 jobs. Its boss says higher gambling taxes have changed the business model of the UK betting industry.", "lead_zh": "Paddy Power、Sky Bet和Betfair的母公司Flutter宣布最多裁员1400人。公司老板表示，博彩税上涨已经改变了英国博彩业的商业模式。", "preview": "Flutter, which owns Paddy Power, Sky Bet and Betfair, said it would cut up to 1,400 jobs because it \"cannot fully absorb\" the tax rises impo", "preview_zh": "拥有Paddy Power、Sky Bet和Betfair的Flutter表示，由于公司“无法完全消化”对博彩业加征的税收，将最多裁员1400人。受影响最大的是利兹和都柏林的员工，以及在葡萄牙和罗马尼亚为英国和爱尔兰业务工作的员工，但具体哪些岗位面临风险尚未公布。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 712, "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/73/en_b2.mp3", "duration": 100.475, "size_bytes": 603792, "engine": "kokoro", "voice": "af_heart", "word_count": 293, "has_timeline": true, "alternates": [{"voice": "af_bella", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/73/en_b2_af_bella.mp3", "duration": 103.575, "size_bytes": 622368, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 293, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/73/en_b2_af_bella.json"}, {"voice": "am_michael", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/73/en_b2_am_michael.mp3", "duration": 109.15, "size_bytes": 655920, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 293, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/73/en_b2_am_michael.json"}, {"voice": "bf_emma", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/73/en_b2_bf_emma.mp3", "duration": 93.95, "size_bytes": 564624, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 293, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/73/en_b2_bf_emma.json"}, {"voice": "bm_george", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/73/en_b2_bm_george.mp3", "duration": 101.15, "size_bytes": 607824, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 293, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/73/en_b2_bm_george.json"}]}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@6d534c3/content/data/versions/724.json", "paragraphs": ["Flutter, which owns Paddy Power, Sky Bet and Betfair, said it would cut up to 1,400 jobs because it \"cannot fully absorb\" the tax rises imposed on the gambling industry. Staff in Leeds and Dublin, as well as UK and Ireland workers at the company's sites in Portugal and Romania, will be most affected, though the roles at risk have not been disclosed.", "The government announced higher taxes on online casino and sports betting in last year's Budget, with an exemption for horse racing. Flutter boss Kevin Harrington said the increases had \"fundamentally changed\" the economics of the UK betting industry and had helped \"fuel the unlicensed, unregulated market\". Some of the tax rises took effect in April.", "Flutter employs 28,500 people worldwide, including 9,000 in the UK and Ireland, and the BBC understands that staff in London, Sunderland, Malta and Gibraltar could also be affected. The restructuring plan will cost between $80m and $90m. A government spokesperson called the cuts a \"commercial decision for Flutter, not the UK government\", but said ministers understood it was a difficult time for workers.", "The company reported a $299m pre-tax loss for the three months to June, compared with a $205m profit a year earlier, although sales rose 3% to $4.3bn. Revenue in the UK and Ireland grew 4%, helped by strong online gambling games. Flutter left the London Stock Exchange in August and now trades only in New York, while rival Entain has also cut jobs."], "paragraphs_zh": ["拥有Paddy Power、Sky Bet和Betfair的Flutter表示，由于公司“无法完全消化”对博彩业加征的税收，将最多裁员1400人。受影响最大的是利兹和都柏林的员工，以及在葡萄牙和罗马尼亚为英国和爱尔兰业务工作的员工，但具体哪些岗位面临风险尚未公布。", "政府在去年的预算中宣布提高在线赌场和体育博彩的税收，但对赛马给予豁免。Flutter老板凯文·哈林顿表示，加税“从根本上改变”了英国博彩业的经济模式，还助长了“无牌照、不受监管的市场”。部分加税措施已于4月生效。", "Flutter在全球拥有28500名员工，其中9000人在英国和爱尔兰。BBC了解到，伦敦、桑德兰、马耳他和直布罗陀的员工也可能受到影响。重组计划将耗资8000万至9000万美元。一位政府发言人表示，裁员是“Flutter的商业决定，而非英国政府的决定”，但称政府理解这对员工来说是一段艰难时期。", "公司报告称，截至6月的三个月税前亏损2.99亿美元，而去年同期盈利2.05亿美元，不过销售额增长3%至43亿美元。受在线博彩游戏强劲增长的推动，英国和爱尔兰的收入增长了4%。Flutter已于8月从伦敦证券交易所退市，目前仅在纽约交易，竞争对手Entain也已裁员。"], "body": "Flutter, which owns Paddy Power, Sky Bet and Betfair, said it would cut up to 1,400 jobs because it \"cannot fully absorb\" the tax rises imposed on the gambling industry. Staff in Leeds and Dublin, as well as UK and Ireland workers at the company's sites in Portugal and Romania, will be most affected, though the roles at risk have not been disclosed.\n\nThe government announced higher taxes on online casino and sports betting in last year's Budget, with an exemption for horse racing. Flutter boss Kevin Harrington said the increases had \"fundamentally changed\" the economics of the UK betting industry and had helped \"fuel the unlicensed, unregulated market\". Some of the tax rises took effect in April.\n\nFlutter employs 28,500 people worldwide, including 9,000 in the UK and Ireland, and the BBC understands that staff in London, Sunderland, Malta and Gibraltar could also be affected. The restructuring plan will cost between $80m and $90m. A government spokesperson called the cuts a \"commercial decision for Flutter, not the UK government\", but said ministers understood it was a difficult time for workers.\n\nThe company reported a $299m pre-tax loss for the three months to June, compared with a $205m profit a year earlier, although sales rose 3% to $4.3bn. Revenue in the UK and Ireland grew 4%, helped by strong online gambling games. Flutter left the London Stock Exchange in August and now trades only in New York, while rival Entain has also cut jobs.", "body_zh": "拥有Paddy Power、Sky Bet和Betfair的Flutter表示，由于公司“无法完全消化”对博彩业加征的税收，将最多裁员1400人。受影响最大的是利兹和都柏林的员工，以及在葡萄牙和罗马尼亚为英国和爱尔兰业务工作的员工，但具体哪些岗位面临风险尚未公布。\n\n政府在去年的预算中宣布提高在线赌场和体育博彩的税收，但对赛马给予豁免。Flutter老板凯文·哈林顿表示，加税“从根本上改变”了英国博彩业的经济模式，还助长了“无牌照、不受监管的市场”。部分加税措施已于4月生效。\n\nFlutter在全球拥有28500名员工，其中9000人在英国和爱尔兰。BBC了解到，伦敦、桑德兰、马耳他和直布罗陀的员工也可能受到影响。重组计划将耗资8000万至9000万美元。一位政府发言人表示，裁员是“Flutter的商业决定，而非英国政府的决定”，但称政府理解这对员工来说是一段艰难时期。\n\n公司报告称，截至6月的三个月税前亏损2.99亿美元，而去年同期盈利2.05亿美元，不过销售额增长3%至43亿美元。受在线博彩游戏强劲增长的推动，英国和爱尔兰的收入增长了4%。Flutter已于8月从伦敦证券交易所退市，目前仅在纽约交易，竞争对手Entain也已裁员。", "text": "Flutter, which owns Paddy Power, Sky Bet and Betfair, said it would cut up to 1,400 jobs because it \"cannot fully absorb\" the tax rises imposed on the gambling industry. Staff in Leeds and Dublin, as well as UK and Ireland workers at the company's sites in Portugal and Romania, will be most affected, though the roles at risk have not been disclosed. The government announced higher taxes on online casino and sports betting in last year's Budget, with an exemption for horse racing. Flutter boss Kevin Harrington said the increases had \"fundamentally changed\" the economics of the UK betting industry and had helped \"fuel the unlicensed, unregulated market\". Some of the tax rises took effect in April. Flutter employs 28,500 people worldwide, including 9,000 in the UK and Ireland, and the BBC understands that staff in London, Sunderland, Malta and Gibraltar could also be affected. The restructuring plan will cost between $80m and $90m. A government spokesperson called the cuts a \"commercial decision for Flutter, not the UK government\", but said ministers understood it was a difficult time for workers. The company reported a $299m pre-tax loss for the three months to June, compared with a $205m profit a year earlier, although sales rose 3% to $4.3bn. Revenue in the UK and Ireland grew 4%, helped by strong online gambling games. Flutter left the London Stock Exchange in August and now trades only in New York, while rival Entain has also cut jobs.", "vocab": [{"word": "absorb", "pos": "verb", "zh": "消化，承受", "note": "常与成本、冲击搭配，如 absorb costs", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "impose", "pos": "verb", "zh": "强加，征收", "note": "impose a tax on sth 对某物征税", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "exemption", "pos": "noun", "zh": "豁免，免除", "note": "exemption for sth 对某事物的豁免", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "fundamentally", "pos": "adv", "zh": "从根本上", "note": "强调变化的程度很深", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "unregulated", "pos": "adj", "zh": "不受监管的", "note": "un- + regulated，反义为 regulated", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "disclose", "pos": "verb", "zh": "披露，公布", "note": "常用被动：has not been disclosed", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "restructure", "pos": "verb", "zh": "重组", "note": "名词形式为 restructuring", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "pre-tax loss", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "税前亏损", "note": "财经报道常见搭配，与 profit 相对", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "revenue", "pos": "noun", "zh": "收入，营收", "note": "公司层面的收入，常用不可数", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "delist", "pos": "verb", "zh": "退市", "note": "delist from a stock exchange", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "spokesperson", "pos": "noun", "zh": "发言人", "note": "中性词，可指男女发言人", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "rival", "pos": "noun", "zh": "竞争对手", "note": "也可作形容词，如 rival company", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}], "title_original": "Paddy Power cuts 1,400 jobs and blames betting tax rises", "summary_original": "The government increased taxes on online casino and sports betting in last year's Budget.", "body_original": "Paddy Power cuts 1,400 jobs and blames betting tax rises\nBy\nMichael Race\nBusiness reporter\nPublished\n20 October 2026\nPaddy Power-owner Flutter has announced plans to cut up to 1,400 jobs as its boss claimed the company \"cannot fully absorb\" tax rises imposed on the gambling industry.\nStaff based in Leeds and Dublin, as well as workers for its UK and Ireland business at Flutter's Portugal and Romania sites, will be most affected, but what roles are at risk has not been disclosed.\nThe government announced taxes rises on online casino and sports betting, with an exemption for horse racing, in the Budget last year.\nFlutter boss Kevin Harrington said the tax hikes had \"fundamentally changed\" the economic model of the UK betting and gaming industry, arguing it had helped \"fuel the unlicensed, unregulated market\".\n\"We continue to expect these tax increases to have a very significant impact on the overall market,\" Flutter Entertainment said on Tuesday.\nFlutter, which also owns Sky Bet and Betfair, employs 28,500 people across the world, including 9,000 in the UK and Ireland.\nAs well as its Leeds and Dublin offices, the BBC understands the cuts could also affect staff based in London and Sunderland, as well as Malta and Gibraltar.\nHarrington, who is chief executive of the betting giant's UK and Ireland business, said: \"As we warned a year ago, we cannot fully absorb a rise of this magnitude without reducing our fixed cost base and therefore must restructure our business so that we can best position ourselves for the future.\"\nA government spokesperson said the job cuts were a \"commercial decision for Flutter, not the UK government\".\n\"However, we understand this will be a difficult time for the workers,\" they added.\nFlutter delisted from the London Stock Exchange in August in a blow to the UK, with its shares now solely traded in New York.\nIn its most recent results, the company reported a $299m (£224m) pre-tax loss for the three months to June for its entire business worldwide, compared to a $205m profit in the same period last year. Sales rose 3% to $4.3bn.\nHowever, revenues in the UK and Ireland rose by 4% over the period, due to strong growth in online gambling games.\nSome online gambling tax rises announced in last year's Budget took effect in April. This included remote gaming duty, which is paid on online casino betting, rising from 21% to 40%.\nGeneral betting duty, paid on the profits made from various forms of sports betting, was kept at 15% in betting shops, but is set to rise from 15% to 25% online in April next year.\nBetting firms had warned that cost increases would lead to job losses and betting shop closures, but\nMPs dismissed the warnings as \"scaremongering\".\nDuring the summer, Ladbrokes owner Entain announced job cuts, with news agency Reuters reporting 500 roles were being removed.\nPunters' winnings from gambling are not taxed in the UK, nor is VAT charged on bets.\nFlutter said its restructuring plan would cost between $80m and $90m.\nThe company has claimed in previous financial results that the impact of UK tax rises would hit its underlying profit by $320m this year and $540m in 2027, before any savings or restructure to mitigate the impact.\nRelated topics\nFlutter Entertainment\nCompanies\nGambling\nSports betting\nTax", "fetched_at": "2026-10-21T00:02:22.121369", "timel